==In the manga==
===Pokémon Adventures===
===={{MangaArc|Red, Green & Blue}}====
[[File:Swimmer Adventures.png|thumb|left|150px|A Swimmer in [[Pokémon Adventures]]]]
A Swimmer first appeared in ''[[PS012|Wake Up—You're Snorlax!]]'', participating in the [[Bicycle]] race, during which he was impeded by a [[Snor]]lax sleeping in an inconvenient spot.

===={{MangaArc|Yellow}}====
The Swimmer reappeared in ''[[PS060|Breath of the Dragonair Part 1]]'' and ''[[PS061|Breath of the Dragonair Part 2]]'', where he broke his leg before a surfing contest and lent {{adv|Yellow}} his {{p|Slowpoke}}. A Q&A section of the Netkun website once revealed this Swimmer's name as Akinori.

[[File:Swimmer F Adventures.png|thumb|100px|A female Swimmer in Pokémon Adventures]]
===={{MangaArc|Ruby & Sapphire}}====
{{main|Jack (Adventures)}}
Swimmer {{adv|Jack}} debuted in this arc, trying to look for a {{p|Feebas}}.

===={{MangaArc|Emerald}}====
In ''[[PS305|Interesting Interactions Involving Illumise]]'', {{adv|Emerald}} faced a virtual female Swimmer as his second battle at the {{gdis|Battle Factory|III}}.

===={{MangaArc|Black & White}}====
A male Swimmer was seen amongst the Trainers entering {{OBP|Victory Road|Black and White}} in ''[[PS511|Dream a Little Dream]]''. In the [[PS512|following chapter]], he was shown with a {{p|Seismitoad}}, but was defeated by [[Leo]]'s {{p|Deino}}, eliminating him from the {{un|Pokémon League}} tournament.

